# Bytecode the daemon's python modules produce.
#
# This file is for the LIVE install, where this directory is its OWN git repository and
# the monorepo root .gitignore does not reach it. The fourth corpus is here for a reason
# the other three do not share: the daemon cycle runs its python modules DIRECTLY
# (autoagent/daemon-cycle.sh), never through the bats runner, so the runner's
# bytecode-suppression export never covers this path.
#
# The recovery snapshot screens `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all` per repo
# and refuses the whole run on an untracked __pycache__. A live install happens to hold
# these two rules already — committed to its own recovery repo, but absent from the
# source repo and from the manifest, so it has no shipped origin and a NEW install would
# reproduce the refusal. Shipping the file is what closes that.
#
# Monorepo-wide rules stay in the root .gitignore — this is a shipped per-repo artifact,
# not a second place to add them.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
